MIT LICENSE for PROTON
======================

PROTON consists of the following tools:-
1. "bracer": adds braces around C statements
2. "instrumenter": instruments the C code with assertions for non-termination checking using CBMC 
3. CBMC --- the C Bounded Model checker, available at https://github.com/diffblue/cbmc
4. Z3 : the Z3 SMT solver available at https://github.com/Z3Prover/z3
5. Glucose : the Glucose SAT solver available at https://github.com/audemard/glucose
6. WITNESS: this utility is implemented in parse_trace_vf.py; it converts CBMC's counterexample trace to the graphml format
7. proton: a shell script that all glues all the above for termination and non-termination checking.
8. Llama and its dependencies


Of the above, 1 , 2, and 7 are our contributions, and we use MIT license for them just like CBMC.
 Item 6, WITNESS, developed by TATA Consultancy Services, is also bound by MIT License and is a part of this repository.

CBMC, Z3 and Glucose are bound by their respective licenses found on their respective repository site, which we have replicated in this repository.

Llama and its dependencies are listed in llm-dependencies.LICENSE. This contains the licenses of Llamma3.2-1b-instruct, and all our dependennt software including Llama.cpp and llama-cpp-python.


